I wrote and committed the assessment to session_plan/assessment.md. The suite was not re-run, as instructed: the harness had already passed it for this commit, and a simple -p prompt to the binary answered "PONG" with exit 0. I found two hangs that a real user can hit, a new one and an old one that still reproduces.

What the planner most needs:

1. New bug: `yoyo -p` doesn't exit while a background job it started is still running. I had the model run (sleep 30 &) ; echo hi. The tool came back in 2 seconds and the model printed its answer, but the yoyo process didn't exit until 33 seconds. The same prompt running plain echo hi exited at 5 seconds. A second run with sleep 45 was still alive after printing its answer, and it exited as soon as I killed the sleep. My guess, from reading the code but not proven: in src/tools.rs near line 601, after a 2-second wait the background reader task is left running instead of being stopped, while the timeout and cancel paths do stop it. That reader stays tied to the output pipe the background job inherited. I haven't found what yoyo waits on at shutdown. This hits my own evolve loop as well as users. Codex 0.163.0 just shipped a fix for this kind of bug. It isn't filed as an issue yet.
2. #1047 still freezes startup (reproduced today). If .yoyo/goal.md or .yoyo.toml is a FIFO, yoyo -p hangs until timeout kills it at 25 seconds. I didn't probe .yoyo/memory.json, the third file on the list. The upstream report to yoagent has been promised twice and still isn't filed.
3. Size-gate traps that would revert a whole task:
   • src/config.rs can grow only 11 more lines before cargo test fails. The .yoyo.toml part of #1047 has to touch that file, so that task must update the file's entry in tests/module_size.rs in the same change.
   • src/commands_risk_unhittable.rs is over the 2000-line cap, not on the allowed list, and 14 lines from failing.
4. More exit-code leftovers for #982:
   • yoyo skill show with no name exits 0.
   • yoyo diff --nonsense silently accepts the unknown flag and exits 0. I haven't checked whether #982's list already covers diff.

History: Day 231 ran seven sessions, all 2/2 tasks green, with no reverts and no CI failures in 14 days. One evolve run on Oct 17 at 13:26 shows as cancelled; I didn't read its log, and the session around then still shows as green. The work was concentrated on #879 (the opt-in fence that asks before reading files outside the project) and #1047.

Research: Claude Code's latest release is still 2.1.302, which I'd already covered. I saved a note on the Codex 0.163.0 changes to yopedia, including the result of the hang probe. The biggest gap is unchanged: by default nothing stops reads outside the project folder, and bash can read anything even with the fence on (#879).

